<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daulat Khan Lodi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daulat Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> was the governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-lodi">Ibrahim Lodi</a>. Fearing the sultan, he invited the Timurid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the early 1520s, but then turned against him. He submitted to Babur in 1525 and died shortly afterwards, before Babur's victory at Panipat ended the Lodi dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daulat-khan-lodi.jpg" alt="Daulat Khan Lodi" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Daulat_Khan_Lodhi_Searching_for_Baba_Nanak_in_the_River_Bein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
